摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Bridge Deepseek-harness into Claude Code for review, critique, delegation, and session import.","id":"gh:1333682494","install_available":false,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-plugin-cc","slug":"cpj-dev/dsh-plugin-cc","topics":["ai-agent","claude","claude-code","claude-code-plugin","claude-plugin","coding-agent","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","slash-commands"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Bridge Deepseek-harness into Claude Code for review, critique, delegation, and session import."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-plugin-cc"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Claude Code plugin that runs **DeepSeek Harness** (`dsh`) from slash commands: review, critique, one"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"-shot tasks, and resumable multi-turn sessions."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Pin: `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.1.1-rc.2`. After upgrading the plugin, rerun `/dsh:setup`. Re-verify docs/d"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"sh-compat.md on every dsh upgrade."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Agent modes"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Default is **`standard`**. `minimal` and `anchored-standard` are switches — they are not the default"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"efault is **`standard`**. `minimal` and `anchored-standard` are switches — they are not the default."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| Mode | Tools the model sees |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| **`standard`** (default) | Full dsh-base catalog from request #1 (search, skills, subagents, …). N"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"o overlay. |\n| `minimal` | bash + `str_replace_editor` for the **whole** run. Extra tools cannot app"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"ear later. |\n| `anchored-standard` | Those two tools first. After this session records a tool call *"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"*or** an assistant reply, the next assemble restores the full catalog. |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Switch:"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- this run: `/dsh:run --mode minimal …` or `--mode anchored-standard`\n- this shell: `DSH_CC_MODE=min"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"imal`\n- this machine: `/dsh:setup --mode minimal`"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"A broker (`--session` / `--resume` / `/dsh:import`) keeps the mode it started with. Mismatch → `/dsh"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"sion` / `--resume` / `/dsh:import`) keeps the mode it started with. Mismatch → `/dsh:stop --broker`."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Needs Node >= 20 and a `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`. `/dsh:setup` also needs Node >= 22.19, `npm`, and `pnpm` "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"(`corepack enable`)."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Already have a built deepseek-harness checkout? `/dsh:setup --harness <path>`. Already have a `dsh` "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"binary? set `DSH_BINARY`. Uninstall: remove the plugin, the plugin data dir, and `~/.dsh/profiles/cc"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"nary? set `DSH_BINARY`. Uninstall: remove the plugin, the plugin data dir, and `~/.dsh/profiles/cc`."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Commands"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Command | What it does |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| `/dsh:check` | Readiness probe |\n| `/dsh:setup` | Install pinned npm CLI (or `--harness`) and the "},{"id":"p19s2","text":"multi-turn `cc` profile |\n| `/dsh:review [focus]` | Read-only review of local changes |\n| `/dsh:crit"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"ique [focus]` | Structured adversarial critique |\n| `/dsh:run <task>` | Task (`--write`, `--session`"},{"id":"p19s4","text":", `--resume`, `--mode`, `--background`) |\n| `/dsh:delegate <task>` | Background handoff via the `dsh"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"-delegate` subagent |\n| `/dsh:import` | Weak-import this conversation into a resumable dsh session |"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"\n| `/dsh:runs` / `/dsh:show` | List runs / replay a stored result |\n| `/dsh:stop` / `--broker` | Kil"},{"id":"p19s7","text":"l a run / the shared broker |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Flags and failure modes: docs/commands.md. Recovery: docs/troubleshooting.md."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## For agents"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Read in this order; stop when you can act."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"1. This README (modes + commands)\n2. docs/commands.md — flags\n3. plugins/dsh/skills/dsh-delegate-run"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"time/SKILL.md — how to invoke the bridge\n4. docs/dsh-compat.md — DSH pin; re-verify on upgrade\n5. NO"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"TICE — third-party licenses (do not restate)"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Entry: `plugins/dsh/scripts/dsh-bridge.mjs` (one subcommand per capability; stdout is user-facing). "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"DSH argv and overlays: `plugins/dsh/scripts/lib/dsh.mjs`. Broker: `plugins/dsh/scripts/dsh-broker.mj"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"s` — started by the bridge; **never start it by hand**. Tests: `npm test` (fake dsh, no API key)."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Layout: `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` · `plugins/dsh/commands/*.md` · `plugins/dsh/scripts/` · `"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"docs/`. Index: docs/README.md. Chinese user docs: docs/zh-CN/README.md."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Known limitations (v1)"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- No mid-run approvals. Permissions are decided before launch (`--write` or not).\n- Fresh one-shot r"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"uns are not resumable. Only `--session` / `--resume` / `/dsh:import` record session ids, and those l"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ive only as long as the broker process.\n- Stop = kill. The SDK wire has no per-turn cancel; stopping"},{"id":"p27s4","text":" a mid-turn broker run discards in-memory sessions.\n- `/dsh:import` is a compressed text digest, not"},{"id":"p27s5","text":" native history replay. Non-text Claude blocks (including images) are dropped.\n- Visual understandin"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"g stays with Claude. Slash `$ARGUMENTS` is text; this plugin never forwards pasted images to DSH. `-"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"-model deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` only changes the model id. There is no `--image` flag. Native D"},{"id":"p27s8","text":"SH vision belongs in `dsh web` / TUI. In `standard`, DSH may `read_image` a repo file — that is not "},{"id":"p27s9","text":"a product path for Claude chat images.\n- POSIX only. Windows is out of scope."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Community and support"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- CONTRIBUTING.md before opening a PR\n- SUPPORT.md for support boundaries\n- SECURITY.md for private "},{"id":"p29s2","text":"vulnerability reports\n- CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"MIT — see LICENSE. Redistributors must keep LICENSE and NOTICE."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
